Signing keys for the sample programs (Ed25519 seeds, 64 hex digits). They are NOT in the repository: tools/mkmap.py makes them
the first time it runs, so every checkout has its own.

dev.seed    the key the system image trusts (its public half is written to /system/etc/program-keys by tools/mkmap.py)
rogue.seed  a key the system does NOT trust: signs the `rogue` test package, which the program manager must refuse

A real deployment keeps its signing key off the build machine and puts only the public key into /system/etc/program-keys.
